--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8457553d7570b1146a94bd661e6d7528, type: 3}
  m_Name: Rule of Law Mission
  missionName: Rule of Law
  description: "The political system is being tested precisely because powerful people dislike what it has produced. Resolve 1 faction demand through the lawful constitutional process and preserve the principle that disputes over authority are settled by institutions rather than force."
  flavorText: "The constitution is easiest to defend when everyone agrees with its outcome. Its real test comes when factions with genuine power believe the rules have failed them. {FactionName} now demands: {Demand}. Opponents insist that accepting the demand would itself weaken the political order, while supporters argue that refusing it would prove that ordinary institutions are incapable of responding. The government will not settle the dispute through soldiers, intimidation, or a permanent suspension of procedure. Courts, legislatures, elections, councils, or other lawful institutions must produce an answer that even the disappointed can recognize as legitimate."
  splashImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a073bc5106fe9c34e9016e27ec8993ea, type: 3}
  victorySplashImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 54525d0469bc17c4ca45371b8a21af6b, type: 3}
  failureSplashImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 2d366369883f3f0429957ef6552cede2, type: 3}
  victoryFlavorText: "The demand was resolved through lawful procedure, and even disappointed factions must now confront a legitimate result instead of an imposed one. Courts, councils, and assemblies proved they could still convert conflict into decisions. Public confidence does not become universal overnight, but the constitutional order regains practical authority. Rule of law survives because it was used under pressure, not merely praised in calm."
  failureFlavorText: "Lawful institutions could not deliver a settlement before the window closed. Procedural delays, tactical obstruction, and factional distrust convinced too many actors that legality was only theater. Extra-constitutional pressure now appears more effective than constitutional process. A system that cannot decide in crisis invites those who promise decisions without it."
  participantRole: 0
  strategyTags: 80
  objectives:
  - objectiveName: Rule of Law
    description: "Resolve 1 faction demand through the constitutional political system."
    type: 37
    targetValue: 1
    targetMode: 0
    targetMultiplier: 1
    minimumTarget: 0
    maximumTarget: 0
  constraints: []
  rewardTiers:
  - tierName: Complete
    requiredObjectivesCompleted: 1
    rewardLegacy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4717193136db46789dcc8cfa28caad2a, type: 2}
